// M1 — Marketing and generative AI — Final assessment (without AI). Questions not used in the previous sessions.
$CATEGORY: Master/Marketing/Final assessment

::Benefit segmentation::Grouping runners by what they seek in a shoe (performance, comfort, ethics, style) is an example of…{=benefit segmentation ~geographic segmentation ~demographic segmentation ~price segmentation}

::Target choice::Which argument best justifies choosing a target segment?{=It is large enough, reachable, and the brand has a credible advantage there ~It is the segment the CEO likes best ~It contains every runner in the country ~It is the segment with the lowest income}

::Positioning statement::Which of these is a complete positioning statement?{=For urban runners who care about their impact, Stride is the everyday running shoe with a recycled upper that lasts as long as conventional ones, because it is tested to 800 km ~Stride, run green! ~Stride shoes are on sale now in all our shops ~Stride is the best shoe in the world}

::Three Ds::Which three criteria should a point of difference meet?{=Desirable, deliverable, distinctive ~Cheap, fast, visible ~Green, global, generic ~Short, simple, funny}

::Perceptual gap::On a perceptual map, an empty area between competitors means…{=a possible positioning opportunity, if consumers actually value it ~that the market does not exist ~that prices are too high ~that the axes are wrongly chosen}

::Allowed claim::Which claim is acceptable under EU rules on environmental claims?{=Jacket made from 80 % recycled polyester (Global Recycled Standard certified) ~100 % sustainable jacket ~Climate-neutral jacket thanks to our carbon offsets ~The planet's favourite jacket}

::AI proposals::A generative AI suggests the positioning "the zero-impact running shoe". What should a junior marketer do first?{=Check whether the product can prove that claim, and reject or rewrite it if not ~Use it as it is because it was generated by AI ~Add it to the packaging ~Translate it into several languages}

::Break-even::Fixed costs are 200 000 €, the price is 100 € and the unit variable cost is 60 €. How many units must be sold to break even?{#5000}

::Price premium::Which evidence best supports a price premium for recycled running shoes?{=Tests showing that the target segment is willing to pay more for verified benefits ~The fact that recycled materials cost more ~A competitor's price cut ~The CEO's personal preference}

::Launch KPI::Which of these is a measurable KPI for a launch?{=Sell-through rate of 60 % in the first three months ~Increase brand awareness ~Make customers happy ~Be more sustainable}
